 ## Overview
-The GPU-based Fast Hartley Transform (FHT) is a frequency-domain volume rendering method that replaces the Fourier transform with the Hartley transform to map real-valued input data directly to real-valued spectra [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. This reduces memory requirements by half compared to the standard GPU-based Fourier transform [S1, S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Hartley Transform for Memory Reduction](895-hartley-transform-for-memory-reduction.md) by providing a specific GPU shader implementation using double butterfly passes and dual lookup textures.
